{"id":"spl-rub.2","title":"PARSE-2: Implement expression parser (Pratt)","description":"Implement Pratt parser for expressions with precedence.\n\n## Testing Pattern\n\nUse expect-test for snapshot testing of parsed AST trees.\n\n### Test Helper (in parser module)\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n    use expect_test::Expect;\n\n    pub fn check(input: \u0026str, expected_tree: \u0026Expect) {\n        let mut parser = Parser::new(input);\n        _ = parser.parse_expr().expect(\"Error while parsing expression\");\n\n        let parse = parser.finish_parse();\n        expected_tree.assert_eq(\u0026parse.debug_tree());\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Example Tests (expr/binary.rs)\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use crate::syntax::parser::expressions::tests::check;\n    use expect_test::expect;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn simple_binary_expr() {\n        check(\n            \"1+2\",\n            \u0026expect![[r#\"\n                BinaryExpr@0..3\n                  Literal@0..1\n                    DecimalInteger@0..1 \"1\"\n                  Operator@1..2\n                    Plus@1..2 \"+\"\n                  Literal@2..3\n                    DecimalInteger@2..3 \"2\"\"#]],\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn left_associative_binary_expr() {\n        check(\n            \"1+2+3+4\",\n            \u0026expect![[r#\"\n                BinaryExpr@0..7\n                  BinaryExpr@0..5\n                    BinaryExpr@0..3\n                      Literal@0..1\n                        DecimalInteger@0..1 \"1\"\n                      Operator@1..2\n                        Plus@1..2 \"+\"\n                      Literal@2..3\n                        DecimalInteger@2..3 \"2\"\n                    Operator@3..4\n                      Plus@3..4 \"+\"\n                    Literal@4..5\n                      DecimalInteger@4..5 \"3\"\n                  Operator@5..6\n                    Plus@5..6 \"+\"\n                  Literal@6..7\n                    DecimalInteger@6..7 \"4\"\"#]],\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn mixed_binding_power_binary_expr() {\n        check(\n            \"1+2*3-4\",\n            \u0026expect![[r#\"\n                BinaryExpr@0..7\n                  BinaryExpr@0..5\n                    Literal@0..1\n                      DecimalInteger@0..1 \"1\"\n                    Operator@1..2\n                      Plus@1..2 \"+\"\n                    BinaryExpr@2..5\n                      Literal@2..3\n                        DecimalInteger@2..3 \"2\"\n                      Operator@3..4\n                        Asterisk@3..4 \"*\"\n                      Literal@4..5\n                        DecimalInteger@4..5 \"3\"\n                  Operator@5..6\n                    Hyphen@5..6 \"-\"\n                  Literal@6..7\n                    DecimalInteger@6..7 \"4\"\"#]],\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- expect-test crate already added to dev-dependencies\n- Use `cargo test` then `UPDATE_EXPECT=1 cargo test` to update snapshots\n- Tree format shows SyntaxKind@start..end with hierarchical indentation","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"matt@remmel.dev","created_at":"2026-01-20T10:16:59.319262-05:00","created_by":"Matthew Remmel","updated_at":"2026-01-20T12:16:11.917147-05:00","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"spl-rub.2","depends_on_id":"spl-rub","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-01-20T10:16:59.319758-05:00","created_by":"Matthew Remmel"},{"issue_id":"spl-rub.2","depends_on_id":"spl-rub.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-01-20T10:19:08.993291-05:00","created_by":"Matthew Remmel"},{"issue_id":"spl-rub.2","depends_on_id":"spl-02h.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-01-20T10:19:09.054036-05:00","created_by":"Matthew Remmel"}]}
